.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_unset_alias(bc_client_t *c, const char *name);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a shell alias from the bash\-server session associated with the
client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
After a successful call, the alias no longer exists in the session\(cqs
alias table.
.PP
The function sends an \f[CR]unset\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqalias\(dq\f[R] and the given alias name.
The server performs the equivalent of \f[CR]unalias name\f[R] in the
shell session.
.PP
If the alias does not exist, the server treats this as a successful
operation (no error is returned).
This provides idempotent behavior, allowing callers to remove aliases
without first checking whether they are defined.
